window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-9eaf251f273c9bc9"]={"zh":"<h1 id=\"chatgpt-space\">ChatGPT Space（空间）</h1> <blockquote> <p>完整文档索引见 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在页面 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该页面的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p>ChatGPT Space 将你的页面、幻灯片、文件和共享工作汇集到一处。 你可以与 ChatGPT 一起编写和编辑内容，然后邀请其他人协作。</p> <blockquote> <p>插图：ChatGPT Space 中包含页面、协作式幻灯片、模板和共享启动计划。将指针移到插图上，可以看到标有“You（你）”的光标。</p> </blockquote> <p><a href=\"https://chatgpt.com/space\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">在 ChatGPT 中打开 Space（需联网）</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"workspaces-and-spaces\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"space\">工作区与 Space</h2> <p>你的 <strong>ChatGPT 工作区</strong>是你登录的个人或组织环境。它决定你的成员身份、设置和可用应用。 Space 中包含你在该环境中可以访问的工作内容。</p> <p>在 Space 中，一个<strong>空间</strong>会围绕某个主题或团队（例如设计工作室或研究项目）组织页面。共享该空间即可让协作者访问其中的页面。你也可以单独创建页面。</p> <blockquote> <p>插图：Space 侧边栏包含 Pages、Sites、Images 和 Google Drive，并列出已保存的工作。</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"pages-and-other-content\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_1\">页面和其他内容</h2> <p><strong><a href=\"#/article/a-c7393fbab700d02d\">页面</a></strong>是你可以与 ChatGPT 一起编辑的文档。 页面可以保存笔记、计划或团队手册，并可包含用于组织相关工作的子页面。 你可以直接编写内容、请 ChatGPT 修改，也可以为协作者留下评论。</p> <p>Space 还可以汇集：</p> <ul> <li><strong><a href=\"#/article/a-71293722d815f9b8?anchor=create-and-refine-slides\">ChatGPT Slides</a>：</strong>根据对话、文件或模板制作演示文稿。你可以与团队和 ChatGPT 一起编辑同一份幻灯片，然后进行演示或导出。</li> <li><strong>电子表格：</strong>使用 ChatGPT 创建和编辑表格并进行计算。</li> <li><strong><a href=\"#/article/a-3c6726ad641677d6\">Sites</a>：</strong>使用 ChatGPT 构建的网站和工具。</li> <li><strong>图片和文件：</strong>上传的文件和已保存的内容，可供打开和重复使用。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"connect-your-sources\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">连接资料来源</h2> <p>Google Drive 等已连接应用可以让 ChatGPT 使用你已有权限访问的文件。将来源链接或文件添加到页面，然后让 ChatGPT 根据这些上下文撰写摘要、进行比较或更新内容。可用来源取决于你的<a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a?anchor=overview\">已连接应用</a>和工作区设置。</p> <p>链接文件会保留其原有权限。你复制或总结到页面上的内容，对能够访问该页面的人可见。共享页面不会共享你的私人聊天或已保存的记忆。</p> <p>要创建第一个页面或幻灯片，请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-71293722d815f9b8\">开始使用</a>。 有关工作区控制，请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-315e17f0f4b919c1\">管理 ChatGPT Space</a>。</p>","en":"<h1 id=\"chatgpt-space\">ChatGPT Space</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <p>ChatGPT Space brings your pages, slides, files, and shared work into one place. Write and edit alongside ChatGPT, then invite other people to work with you.</p> <blockquote> <p>Illustration: ChatGPT Space with pages, collaborative slides, templates, and a shared launch plan. Move your pointer over the illustration to see a cursor labeled You.</p> </blockquote> <p><a href=\"https://chatgpt.com/space\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Open Space in ChatGPT (online)</a>.</p> <h2 id=\"workspaces-and-spaces\">Workspaces and spaces</h2> <p>Your <strong>ChatGPT workspace</strong> is the personal or organization environment you're signed in to. It determines your membership, settings, and available apps. Space holds the work you can access in that environment.</p> <p>Within Space, a <strong>space</strong> groups pages around a topic or team, such as a design studio or a research project. Share the space to give collaborators access to its pages. You can also create a page on its own.</p> <blockquote> <p>Illustration: Space with a sidebar for Pages, Sites, Images, and Google Drive, and a list of saved work.</p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"pages-and-other-content\">Pages and other content</h2> <p>A <strong><a href=\"#/article/a-c7393fbab700d02d\">page</a></strong> is a document you and ChatGPT can edit together. It can hold notes, a plan, or a team handbook, with child pages for related work. You can write directly, ask ChatGPT for revisions, and leave comments for collaborators.</p> <p>Space also brings together:</p> <ul> <li><strong><a href=\"#/article/a-71293722d815f9b8?anchor=create-and-refine-slides\">ChatGPT Slides</a>:</strong> Build a presentation from a conversation, files, or a template. Edit the same deck with your team and ChatGPT, then present or export it.</li> <li><strong>Spreadsheets:</strong> Create and edit tables and calculations with ChatGPT.</li> <li><strong><a href=\"#/article/a-3c6726ad641677d6\">Sites</a>:</strong> Websites and tools you build with ChatGPT.</li> <li><strong>Images and files:</strong> Uploaded files and saved work you can open and reuse.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"connect-your-sources\">Connect your sources</h2> <p>Connected apps, such as Google Drive, let ChatGPT use files you already have access to. Add source links or files to a page, then ask ChatGPT to turn that context into a summary, comparison, or update. Available sources depend on your <a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a?anchor=overview\">connected apps</a> and workspace settings.</p> <p>Linked files keep their original permissions. Content you copy or summarize onto a page is visible to people who can access that page. Sharing a page doesn't share your private chats or saved memory.</p> <p>To create your first page or slide deck, see <a href=\"#/article/a-71293722d815f9b8\">Getting started</a>. For workspace controls, see <a href=\"#/article/a-315e17f0f4b919c1\">Manage ChatGPT Space</a>.</p>"};
